    "one_trade_worth_naming": "movenotes ran with a 1.4 GB write-ahead log, which is one long transaction: fast, and a crash mid-import loses everything. Notrios commits in 3,823 checkpointed batches.",
    "peak_rss_kib": 1279820,
    "seconds": 2186.22,
    "so_the_ratio_is_not_like_for_like": "movenotes produces a staging database that cannot be searched; Notrios produces a searchable library. The comparison bounds how much of the import time is inherent -- walking 1,237,553 files and parsing Joplin items -- rather than showing the same job done better.",
    "source": "cloned from github.com/renesugar/movenotes-v3, not the owner's working copy",
    "tool": "movenotes-v3 joplin2sql",
    "what_it_builds": "two tables -- settings and notes -- with eight B-tree indexes and no full-text index. Every RAW item becomes one row.",
    "what_notrios_builds_instead": "382,206 notes with revision chains, a documents_fts index whose data alone is 374 MB, a link index, 781 notebooks, 11,753 tags with 842,813 tag applications, and a content-addressed asset store."
  },
